The  driver  utilizes the driver to provide a system bell with or
without a keyboard for the framework.  When a bell  character  is
received  on a screen, sounds the bell.  The utility gives access
to several configurable parameters that effect the sound  of  the
system  bell.   The  following  calls are provided by the driver.
Their definitions are found in Will sound the default bell.  Will
return a struct wskbd_bell_data with the current bell parameters.
Takes a struct wskbd_bell_data and uses it to set the bell  para‐
meters.   These  are used by the WSKBDIO_BELL call.  Will sound a
bell using a supplied struct wskbd_bell_data for its  parameters.
Will  return  a  struct wskbd_bell_data with the bell parameters.
